{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Intern Directory Convention.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Intern Directory Convention.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender intern directory convention blender intern directory convention","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Intern Directory Convention.md","fileName":"Blender Intern Directory Convention.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Intern Directory Convention","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Core Source Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Core Source Architecture","Blender Module API Boundary","Blender GHOST Dependency Layer","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Intern Directory Convention.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Intern Directory Convention.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender intern directory convention blender intern directory convention","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Intern Directory Convention.md","fileName":"Blender Intern Directory Convention.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Intern Directory Convention","heading":"Blender Intern Directory Convention","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Many Blender modules place implementation source in an `intern/` subdirectory and public interface headers beside it at the module's top level. Functions inside `intern/` may use static linkage for file-local helpers or external linkage for implementation functions that are still not intended as the public API.\n\nThe arrangement communicates encapsulation even in C. Callers enter through a [[Blender Module API Boundary]], after which the module can descend into specialized internal work without exposing every helper. The same pattern a